      "use": "Definitions of the lattice, links, gauge action, plaquette action and class functions are imported unchanged; theorem result.1 (class-function action invariance) proves part (3) for the constructed gauge.",
      "importance": "Essential: the gauge-fixing statement is about pr-10's gauge action, and the invariance of the Wilson and every class-function action under the fixing is exactly pr-10's theorem."
    }
  ],
  "attribution": {
    "wallet": "0x8562799a4d8AC66F732fd47aF5c20018FF509f8F",
    "contributions": "The Lean construction, statements and proofs were written by an AI coding agent (Claude, Anthropic) on behalf of the wallet holder, who directed the submission. No third-party code is included."
  },
  "limitations": "This is a purely classical, configuration-level statement. It does not prove the Faddeev–Popov identity for the Haar/Wilson measure (Fubini and Haar invariance are not formalized), and it does not construct the transfer matrix. Only τ-links are fixed. Gauge fixing of spatial links (a full maximal-tree gauge) and the residual τ-independent gauge freedom are not treated. Uniqueness of the gauge-fixed form is not proved. Nothing here addresses the quantum theory, the continuum limit or the mass gap."
}
